Report scenarios
Every dossier falls into exactly one of three mutually exclusive scenarios, each
rendered by its own RDLC (existing in _FR and _NL variants):
Unknown client (CONNU = 'N') → rptUnknownClient_{lang}.rdlc
Simple letter, 14 report parameters, no data tables.
Known client, no accounts (CONNU = 'Y' AND FLAG_REKNR = 'N')
→ rptKnownClientNoAccounts_{lang}.rdlc
16 report parameters, no data tables.
Known client, with accounts (CONNU = 'Y' AND FLAG_REKNR = 'Y')
→ rptKnownClientWithAccounts_{lang}.rdlc
The complex path: pulls 8 separate account-type queries (regular accounts,
multi-currency accounts, savings, term deposits, multi-currency term deposits,
pension savings, securities, other products) into a shared XsdDataSet and
binds each as its own ReportDataSource. 25 report parameters, some
conditionally built based on which product tables have data.
Two further templates only attach onto scenario 3, when the client requested a
statement (RELEVS = 'Y'):
rptOverviewAccounts_{lang}.rdlc — transaction overview (also emits a matching
CSV export when the delivery channel is email)
rptOverviewRetirementSavingsAccounts_{lang}.rdlc — retirement savings
transaction overview
When either or both exist, they are merged onto the main scenario-3 PDF (see below)
before delivery — they are not independent client scenarios.
PDF merge and pagination (scenario 3 only)
After rendering, btnGenerate_Click:
Merges any _OverviewAccounts.pdf onto the main PDF via clsManagePdf.MergePdf,
deleting the pieces and renaming the merged temp file back to the canonical name.
Repeats the same merge step for _OverviewRetirementSavingsAccounts.pdf.
Runs clsManagePdf.AddPageNumbers last, so page numbers reflect the final
combined document rather than any individual piece. Updates
TAX_GEN.NR_PAGES with the result.
Mails via MailDocs and routes via MoveToTargetFolder (email output folder,
or print folder bucketed by country BE/non-BE and by page-count "sheets"
subfolder).
Scenarios 1 and 2 skip merge/pagination entirely — they mail and route immediately
after rendering, inside GenerateType1Pdf / GenerateType2Pdf themselves.
