Known quirks worth knowing before changing this code
Mailing happens at different points depending on scenario: scenarios 1 and 2 mail
inside their own GenerateTypeNPdf function; scenario 3 mails from the outer
btnGenerate_Click loop after merge/pagination. Don't assume a single mailing
entry point.
SQL is built via string concatenation (not parameterized), including
user-provided values in frmRequest's add/delete handlers.
Connection strings and DB credentials are base64-encoded, not encrypted —
Encrypt/Decrypt naming is misleading; this is obfuscation only.
Report template paths are hardcoded per-developer Windows username (UINTD,
HOORNR, ES156) with a config-driven fallback (TEMPLATE_PATH) for everyone
else. Any new developer machine needs either a matching username branch or must
rely on the fallback.
intCountReports is calculated once at form load from a combined count across all
three scenarios, then reused as the progress bar maximum across all three
generation loops in sequence — it is not reset per scenario.